  "description": "T1 - T3 - Lime Trees - Tree crowns to be reduced to historical pruning points.  Works to include selective pruning to maintain the natural form and balance of the tree while retaining sufficient healthy furnishing growth for continued vitality and crown continuity.\r\rT4- Sycamore Tree -  the tree will undergo a crown reduction of circa 3 metres in height and 2.5 metres laterally to previous points of reduction.\r\rT5- Mature Cherry Tree - Carry out sensitive crown pruning to improve form, light penetration and overall tree health.  Dead wood will be removed throughout, and neighbouring, lower canopy branch will be cut back to the boundary line to permit more light into the neighbouring property\r\rReason for work: General tree maintenance",
